  <revision rev="2" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>9c6436982dc6c6e8247287700fe05e17</srcmd5>
    <version>0.26.9.29</version>
    <time>1794318037</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>- Update to 0.26.9.29.
  * trash-put no longer leaves a copy of the trashed file in the trash
    directory when a move across filesystem boundaries is blocked by an
    error.
  * Added support for file names that are not valid UTF-8.
  * trash-restore now accepts absolute paths in trash directories that
    are not volume trashes.
  * Removed the &quot;Donate&quot; button.
  * Deleted trashcli/put/same_volume_gate.py.
- Reworked test coverage and tooling:
  * Rewrote trash-restore tests (TrashedFiles, unsafe trash dirs) to run
    through RestoreUser, converted them from unittest to pytest, and
    added tests for trashinfo reading and volume-trashed files.
  * Added IsSymLink and IsStickyDir to FakeFs, added the
    TrashDirHasTrashInfo fixture, and merged RecordingLogger into
    CaptureLogger.
  * Improved type hints and enabled mypy for the tests.
  * Updated dev setup: Docker setup for Python 2.7, editable dev install,
    and version-pinned PyYAML dev requirements.
  * Converted the release docs to Markdown.
</comment>
    <requestid>1396418</requestid>
  </revision>
</revisionlist>
